---
/**
 * The fork tree. This is the site's first content figure, so it also sets the
 * diagram convention: hand-drawn inline SVG in the instrument vocabulary,
 * hairline strokes and accent nodes, animated through the shared
 * `[data-anim-draw]` contract rather than any per-diagram script.
 *
 * Two decisions worth keeping:
 *
 * Geometry only in the SVG, labels in HTML. SVG text scales with the viewBox,
 * so a label legible on a desktop lands at eight or nine pixels on a phone.
 * Keeping the words in HTML lets them use the site's own type tokens and wrap.
 *
 * Five branches, not seventeen. Five is the retropulsion roster the section
 * above prints in full, so the figure and the table describe the same run.
 * Seventeen strands at this size is a smear rather than a diagram.
 */
---
<figure class="fork-tree">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 100 42"
    preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"
    data-anim-draw
    role="img"
    aria-label="A trunk march runs left to right into a pause chosen by the flow. Five branches fan out from that one pause, continue in parallel, and are collected into a single gated verdict."
  >
    <!-- Trunk: one coupled march to the pause. -->
    <line x1="3" y1="21" x2="26" y2="21" pathLength="100" />

    <!-- Fan out, run in parallel, collect. The straight middle segment is the
         point of the figure: the branches are concurrent, not sequential. -->
    <path d="M26,21 C38,21 40,5 52,5"   pathLength="100" />
    <line x1="52" y1="5"  x2="70" y2="5"  pathLength="100" />
    <path d="M70,5  C80,5  80,21 88,21"  pathLength="100" />

    <path d="M26,21 C38,21 40,13 52,13" pathLength="100" />
    <line x1="52" y1="13" x2="70" y2="13" pathLength="100" />
    <path d="M70,13 C80,13 80,21 88,21"  pathLength="100" />

    <path d="M26,21 C38,21 40,29 52,29" pathLength="100" />
    <line x1="52" y1="29" x2="70" y2="29" pathLength="100" />
    <path d="M70,29 C80,29 80,21 88,21"  pathLength="100" />

    <path d="M26,21 C38,21 40,37 52,37" pathLength="100" />
    <line x1="52" y1="37" x2="70" y2="37" pathLength="100" />
    <path d="M70,37 C80,37 80,21 88,21"  pathLength="100" />

    <!-- The committed world runs straight through, which is what committing is. -->
    <line x1="26" y1="21" x2="88" y2="21" pathLength="100" class="committed" />

    <!-- Nodes, in stagger order: the pause, each branch top to bottom, the verdict. -->
    <circle cx="26" cy="21" r="1.5" class="pause" />
    <circle cx="61" cy="5"  r="1" />
    <circle cx="61" cy="13" r="1" />
    <circle cx="61" cy="21" r="1.2" class="committed-node" />
    <circle cx="61" cy="29" r="1" />
    <circle cx="61" cy="37" r="1" />
    <circle cx="88" cy="21" r="1.5" class="verdict" />
  </svg>

  <div class="ft-labels" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="ft-l ft-l-1">One coupled march</span>
    <span class="ft-l ft-l-2">Pause the flow chose</span>
    <span class="ft-l ft-l-3">Branches, concurrent</span>
    <span class="ft-l ft-l-4">One gated verdict</span>
  </div>

  <figcaption>
    Every branch leaves the same pause and shares everything before it. The
    marched state is entered by reference; a branch copies only when it first
    writes.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .fork-tree { margin: var(--space-5) 0; }

  .fork-tree svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 44rem;
    height: auto;
    overflow: visible;
  }

  /* Stroke and fill are scoped per diagram; global.css only carries the
     dash and node timing, never the colour. */
  /* Stroke width is in user units, and `vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke` is
     deliberately absent. It resolves `stroke-dasharray` in device pixels, which
     fights the `pathLength="100"` normalization the draw-in depends on and
     renders every stroke as a dashed line. At the 44rem cap this is about one
     device pixel, which is the hairline the rest of the site uses. */
  .fork-tree line,
  .fork-tree path {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--line-2);
    stroke-width: 0.16;
  }
  .fork-tree line.committed { stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 0.22; }

  .fork-tree circle { fill: var(--fg-2); }
  .fork-tree circle.pause,
  .fork-tree circle.verdict,
  .fork-tree circle.committed-node { fill: var(--accent); }

  .ft-labels {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }
  @media (min-width: 720px) {
    .ft-labels { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); }
  }
  .ft-l {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-eyebrow);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-eyebrow);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--fg-2);
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    color: var(--fg-1);
    font-size: var(--t-body-sm);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
</style>
